WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.874
<c.steel>Episode 4, Touch Move, is not released</c>

2
00:00:04.874 --> 00:00:07.498
<c.steel>yet, and it is on this course anyway,</c>

3
00:00:07.498 --> 00:00:09.234
<c.steel>labelled so.</c>

4
00:00:09.619 --> 00:00:12.440
<c.fact>A brass clock with two dials is set to</c>

5
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.971
<c.fact>fifteen minutes each, and a fountain pen</c>

6
00:00:14.971 --> 00:00:18.878
<c.fact>writes the title on a score sheet: Touch Move.</c>

7
00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:23.286
<c.steel>This much Aaron has decided: a chess lesson</c>

8
00:00:23.286 --> 00:00:25.399
<c.steel>between a passionate teacher and a</c>

9
00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:27.547
<c.steel>nine-year-old boy, with the board at the</c>

10
00:00:27.547 --> 00:00:29.910
<c.steel>centre for the first twenty minutes,</c>

11
00:00:30.136 --> 00:00:32.109
<c.steel>and chess that is interesting</c>

12
00:00:32.109 --> 00:00:34.089
<c.steel>in its own right.</c>

13
00:00:34.486 --> 00:00:37.203
<c.fact>The boy shows how he usually wins:</c>

14
00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.246
<c.fact>Scholar's Mate on his tablet,</c>

15
00:00:39.246 --> 00:00:44.488
<c.fact>against pawn.hab3, which offers him a draw.</c>

16
00:00:44.882 --> 00:00:47.442
<c.fact>Then the teacher makes him Black.</c>

17
00:00:47.494 --> 00:00:51.430
<c.fact>You're a Duke. And a Count. They replay</c>

18
00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:54.797
<c.fact>Morphy's Opera Game of 1858, and the boy</c>

19
00:00:54.797 --> 00:00:58.739
<c.fact>tries to guess each of the Duke's moves first.</c>

20
00:00:59.118 --> 00:01:00.697
<c.fact>At twenty minutes the teacher's</c>

21
00:01:00.697 --> 00:01:02.856
<c.fact>flag falls with his fingertip still</c>

22
00:01:02.856 --> 00:01:04.389
<c.fact>on Morphy's mating rook,</c>

23
00:01:04.389 --> 00:01:05.898
<c.fact>and the whole programme tips</c>

24
00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:09.538
<c.fact>over, like a resigned king.</c>

25
00:01:10.831 --> 00:01:13.269
<c.fact>The teacher is never seen whole,</c>

26
00:01:13.269 --> 00:01:14.924
<c.fact>and never his face.</c>

27
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.424
<c.fact>His name, Daniel Fenn, is written</c>

28
00:01:18.424 --> 00:01:22.691
<c.fact>on an old score sheet, as Black.</c>

29
00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:25.485
<c.steel>Aaron asked for a teacher who loves chess</c>

30
00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:28.666
<c.steel>and loves sharing it, never as a performance,</c>

31
00:01:28.666 --> 00:01:30.501
<c.steel>modelled on Doctor Hiriluk,</c>

32
00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:33.403
<c.steel>from One Piece: never give up on your</c>

33
00:01:33.403 --> 00:01:36.335
<c.steel>imagination when it looks hopeless.</c>

34
00:01:36.717 --> 00:01:40.299
<c.steel>And Aaron decided he is not naive:</c>

35
00:01:40.711 --> 00:01:43.318
<c.steel>he knows when a position is lost.</c>

36
00:01:43.544 --> 00:01:45.935
<c.fact>His only praise, all night,</c>

37
00:01:45.935 --> 00:01:49.599
<c.fact>is one word: Yes.</c>

38
00:01:49.987 --> 00:01:52.251
<c.fact>When the boy says he has used far more</c>

39
00:01:52.251 --> 00:01:55.647
<c.fact>time, he answers: I talk more.</c>

40
00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.742
<c.running>By our reading, he spends his own</c>

41
00:01:57.742 --> 00:02:00.686
<c.running>clock on the boy on purpose.</c>

42
00:02:01.962 --> 00:02:05.909
<c.steel>Aaron has decided who the boy is: nine,</c>

43
00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:09.573
<c.steel>rated about a thousand, never formally taught.</c>

44
00:02:09.984 --> 00:02:12.382
<c.steel>His mother arranged the lesson;</c>

45
00:02:12.794 --> 00:02:15.076
<c.steel>he did not ask for it.</c>

46
00:02:15.466 --> 00:02:19.582
<c.fact>In forty seconds, why do I have to do this,</c>

47
00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.029
<c.fact>becomes: what if I get it right?</c>

48
00:02:24.425 --> 00:02:26.828
<c.fact>His imagination fills the board,</c>

49
00:02:26.828 --> 00:02:29.284
<c.fact>one medium for each kind of piece:</c>

50
00:02:29.452 --> 00:02:32.993
<c.fact>crayon pawns with faces, engraved bishops,</c>

51
00:02:32.993 --> 00:02:35.814
<c.fact>playdough knights, oil-painted queens,</c>

52
00:02:35.814 --> 00:02:39.396
<c.fact>daguerreotype kings and blueprint rooks.</c>

53
00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:42.269
<c.fact>He grabs a pawn, and the teacher says the</c>

54
00:02:42.269 --> 00:02:45.119
<c.fact>rule, the only time in the film:</c>

55
00:02:45.345 --> 00:02:49.833
<c.fact>Touch move. You touched it, you move it.</c>

56
00:02:50.233 --> 00:02:52.671
<c.fact>So he holds the pawn in the air for</c>

57
00:02:52.671 --> 00:02:56.328
<c.fact>forty-two silent seconds, and finds</c>

58
00:02:56.328 --> 00:02:58.796
<c.fact>a better move than the Duke's.</c>

59
00:03:00.092 --> 00:03:03.645
<c.fact>Late in the lesson, the boy asks: Did you</c>

60
00:03:03.645 --> 00:03:09.816
<c.fact>ever give up? And the teacher says: Once.</c>

61
00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.113
<c.fact>I was ten, he says. I had ten minutes on my</c>

62
00:03:14.113 --> 00:03:18.531
<c.fact>clock. He stopped it, and shook her hand.</c>

63
00:03:18.924 --> 00:03:20.776
<c.running>The position is fictional;</c>

64
00:03:21.002 --> 00:03:24.375
<c.running>the crew labelled it so in every file.</c>

65
00:03:24.775 --> 00:03:27.213
<c.fact>The teacher leads him only with questions,</c>

66
00:03:27.213 --> 00:03:31.126
<c.fact>and the boy finds one: Rook c2,</c>

67
00:03:31.126 --> 00:03:34.731
<c.fact>check. If he takes it, I can't move.</c>

68
00:03:34.899 --> 00:03:38.446
<c.fact>If he doesn't, I keep doing it.</c>

69
00:03:38.828 --> 00:03:42.183
<c.fact>Later, at the real table, the boy plays</c>

70
00:03:42.183 --> 00:03:44.784
<c.fact>it out, and the teacher strikes out the</c>

71
00:03:44.784 --> 00:03:47.333
<c.fact>old result and writes in a draw.</c>

72
00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.477
<c.fact>The boy, checking, doesn't see.</c>

73
00:03:51.862 --> 00:03:55.374
<c.egg>White signed the sheet x R.</c>

74
00:03:55.879 --> 00:03:58.474
<c.egg>The film never says who she was:</c>

75
00:03:58.526 --> 00:04:00.889
<c.egg>the signature is a planted egg.</c>

76
00:04:01.057 --> 00:04:02.346
<c.running>By our running count,</c>

77
00:04:02.346 --> 00:04:05.208
<c.running>it was Rosie, at sixteen.</c>

78
00:04:06.502 --> 00:04:09.114
<c.fact>Early on, the boy asks where the captured</c>

79
00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:13.445
<c.fact>pieces go. In the box. And then? And the</c>

80
00:04:13.445 --> 00:04:17.247
<c.fact>teacher says: That's a good question.</c>

81
00:04:17.629 --> 00:04:19.278
<c.fact>At twenty minutes the film</c>

82
00:04:19.278 --> 00:04:20.996
<c.fact>answers by going there,</c>

83
00:04:20.996 --> 00:04:22.703
<c.fact>falling with the night's twelve</c>

84
00:04:22.703 --> 00:04:24.758
<c.fact>captured pieces through the felt,</c>

85
00:04:24.758 --> 00:04:26.935
<c.fact>the stitches and the wood.</c>

86
00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:31.349
<c.fact>Inside the lid is a cross-stitched x R,</c>

87
00:04:31.349 --> 00:04:34.037
<c.fact>its centre the one warm stitch.</c>

88
00:04:34.205 --> 00:04:38.071
<c.fact>Taped beside it, a card: when scared,</c>

89
00:04:38.071 --> 00:04:40.562
<c.fact>twelve in, twenty-four hold,</c>

90
00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.010
<c.fact>twenty-four out, ten hold.</c>

91
00:04:44.403 --> 00:04:46.760
<c.egg>They are the same words as Noor's card on</c>

92
00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:50.771
<c.egg>the Moon, in Episode 2: a planted egg.</c>

93
00:04:51.183 --> 00:04:54.591
<c.open>Why the teacher has them is open.</c>

94
00:04:54.982 --> 00:04:57.234
<c.fact>Down there, the captured pieces keep an</c>

95
00:04:57.234 --> 00:05:00.967
<c.fact>opera house, and the sacrificed queen sings.</c>

96
00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:04.247
<c.fact>At exactly twenty-five minutes, Morphy's</c>

97
00:05:04.247 --> 00:05:10.093
<c.fact>face appears, in oil, for the first time.</c>

98
00:05:11.372 --> 00:05:14.785
<c.open>Who won tonight's game is open: the mate</c>

99
00:05:14.785 --> 00:05:17.915
<c.open>stood on the board, the flag fell first,</c>

100
00:05:17.932 --> 00:05:22.210
<c.open>the hand had not let go, and nobody claimed.</c>

101
00:05:22.604 --> 00:05:26.633
<c.fact>Every draw offer from pawn.hab3 lands two</c>

102
00:05:26.633 --> 00:05:29.750
<c.fact>point five six seconds after the boy's move,</c>

103
00:05:29.976 --> 00:05:32.798
<c.open>and whether it is Episode 2's PAWN,</c>

104
00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:35.904
<c.open>still on the Moon, is open.</c>

105
00:05:36.291 --> 00:05:39.043
<c.fact>At the very end, a small hand accepts</c>

106
00:05:39.043 --> 00:05:41.330
<c.fact>the draw, and the teacher says,</c>

107
00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:45.272
<c.fact>very quietly: Goodnight.</c>

108
00:05:46.568 --> 00:05:48.356
<c.fact>Then Black's flag falls in the</c>

109
00:05:48.356 --> 00:05:50.568
<c.fact>dark, and changes nothing.</c>

110
00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.248
Next: Rosie's life.
